WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.509 --> 00:00:02.028
- All right, let's wrap this hour up

00:00:02.028 --> 00:00:04.110
with an awesome story of
discovery I found online.

00:00:04.110 --> 00:00:05.713
This is what I'm liking.

00:00:05.713 --> 00:00:08.070
(upbeat music)
(audience cheers)

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:10.860
10-year-old Molly is
obsessed with fossils.

00:00:10.860 --> 00:00:13.680
For years, she has scoured the
water's edge in her hometown,

00:00:13.680 --> 00:00:15.990
looking for relics of centuries long past.

00:00:15.990 --> 00:00:18.300
And on Christmas morning,

00:00:18.300 --> 00:00:20.730
Christmas morning, this is crazy.

00:00:20.730 --> 00:00:22.740
She made a once in a lifetime find:

00:00:22.740 --> 00:00:24.720
the tooth of a giant shark

00:00:24.720 --> 00:00:28.080
that roamed the sea 15 million years ago.

00:00:28.080 --> 00:00:29.580
What?

00:00:29.580 --> 00:00:33.210
It's estimated, the
trans-oceanic super predator

00:00:33.210 --> 00:00:36.150
would've been about the
size of a Greyhound bus,

00:00:36.150 --> 00:00:36.983
um-hmm,

00:00:36.983 --> 00:00:39.810
and now one of its chompers
is sitting in Molly's home.

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:40.860
What a life!

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.270
We have her on the line right now

00:00:42.270 --> 00:00:43.560
along with her daddy, Bruce.

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:44.512
What's up y'all?

00:00:44.512 --> 00:00:46.091
(audience cheers)

00:00:46.091 --> 00:00:47.400
- Hey (indistinct)!

00:00:47.400 --> 00:00:49.560
- Molly, you're my hero!

00:00:49.560 --> 00:00:51.150
This is the coolest thing ever.

00:00:51.150 --> 00:00:53.370
I was obsessed with
megalodons and all of that

00:00:53.370 --> 00:00:54.203
when I was a kid.

00:00:54.203 --> 00:00:56.070
So, congrats on this big find.

00:00:56.070 --> 00:00:58.590
What did you think when you discovered it?

00:00:58.590 --> 00:01:01.860
- On Christmas morning, my
dad took me and my sister

00:01:01.860 --> 00:01:04.080
out shark's tooth hunting;

00:01:04.080 --> 00:01:06.390
after we got our waders for Christmas.

00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:11.010
And on Christmas morning we
were in about knee deep water

00:01:11.010 --> 00:01:15.030
and I looked over and I saw
this gigantic megalodon tooth.

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:18.093
And I reached in, I grabbed
it and I was so excited.

00:01:19.200 --> 00:01:20.859
- Yes, so this tooth is-

00:01:20.859 --> 00:01:21.909
(Kelly gasps loudly)
(audience claps)

00:01:21.909 --> 00:01:24.211
Is a megalodon tooth.

00:01:24.211 --> 00:01:25.549
A 5-inch tooth-

00:01:25.549 --> 00:01:27.179
- [Kelly] That is crazy.

00:01:27.179 --> 00:01:29.550
- And what's cool about this
is she's the first human

00:01:29.550 --> 00:01:30.990
to ever hold this tooth.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:32.010
This is just one of many

00:01:32.010 --> 00:01:35.250
in her 400 tooth and fossil
collection that she has.

00:01:35.250 --> 00:01:38.811
- Oh, Molly, you are officially my hero!

00:01:38.811 --> 00:01:39.709
(audience cheers)

00:01:39.709 --> 00:01:41.430
This is so cool.

00:01:41.430 --> 00:01:43.530
So Bruce, y'all actually
had a local museum

00:01:43.530 --> 00:01:44.730
actually help confirm that it was

00:01:44.730 --> 00:01:46.650
a prehistoric shark tooth, right?

00:01:46.650 --> 00:01:49.290
- Yeah, so we know the
curator of paleontology

00:01:49.290 --> 00:01:50.550
at the Calvert Marine Museum,

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.620
and we've been to visit them several times

00:01:52.620 --> 00:01:54.600
to confirm all their finds that we have.

00:01:54.600 --> 00:01:56.010
We actually have a couple
here for you today.

00:01:56.010 --> 00:01:59.070
We have a crocodile teeth here

00:01:59.070 --> 00:01:59.903
and-
- Whoa!

00:01:59.903 --> 00:02:01.200
- Molly's gonna hold this up for you guys.

00:02:01.200 --> 00:02:02.850
And then we also have
a large whale vertebrae

00:02:02.850 --> 00:02:03.750
that we found as well.

00:02:03.750 --> 00:02:06.900
It's actually almost as big as
Molly's head, if not bigger.

00:02:06.900 --> 00:02:08.850
So we've showed that to 'em as well.

00:02:08.850 --> 00:02:10.560
But we took the shark's tooth in there

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:11.700
for them to take a look at

00:02:11.700 --> 00:02:13.930
and they confirmed this megalodon

00:02:14.771 --> 00:02:16.860
and they're blown away how big it is.

00:02:16.860 --> 00:02:18.270
- It is so cool.

00:02:18.270 --> 00:02:20.100
I'm just so excited for you, Molly.

00:02:20.100 --> 00:02:21.360
Oh my gosh.

00:02:21.360 --> 00:02:22.920
I don't know if it goes
up from here, though.

00:02:22.920 --> 00:02:24.660
That's the most amazing find ever.

00:02:24.660 --> 00:02:26.160
Like keep looking, but I mean

00:02:26.160 --> 00:02:28.260
I think you hit the
jackpot right off the bat.

00:02:28.260 --> 00:02:30.330
Thank you so much Molly and Bruce!

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:32.223
I'm liking your face right now-

00:02:33.089 --> 00:02:34.308
(audience claps)

00:02:34.308 --> 00:02:35.141
And that's not all, y'all.

00:02:35.141 --> 00:02:36.690
Are season long partner, Pilot Pen,

00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:39.270
makers of G2, the go-to pen
of "The Kelly Clarkson Show",

00:02:39.270 --> 00:02:42.000
want to honor truly unstoppable
people just like y'all.

00:02:42.000 --> 00:02:43.290
So they're gonna be writing you a check

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:44.280
for a thousand dollars.

00:02:44.280 --> 00:02:45.182
How's that sound?

00:02:45.182 --> 00:02:46.098
(audience cheers)
(Bruce chuckles)

00:02:46.098 --> 00:02:47.240
- Thank you.

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:48.099
- [Kelly] Absolutely.

00:02:48.099 --> 00:02:49.765
- Thank you.
- Thank you guys so much.

00:02:49.765 --> 00:02:51.956
And thank you to all our
guests this hour, Jay Leno,

00:02:51.956 --> 00:02:54.963
Melvin Brown, Dr. Hannah
(indistinct), Dr. Peter Grossman,

00:02:54.963 --> 00:02:57.240
Karen, Alyssa and Amy,
y'all have a great day,

00:02:57.240 --> 00:02:58.990
and if it's not, try and change it.

